---
// Essay-variant specimen: measure on columns 3–9, sidenotes in the margin. Not indexed.
import Periodical from "../layouts/Periodical.astro";
import Kicker from "../components/Kicker.astro";
import Sidenote from "../components/Sidenote.astro";
import SidenoteRef from "../components/SidenoteRef.astro";

const today = new Date(Date.UTC(2026, 9, 11));
---

<Periodical
  title="Essay specimen · As We May Act"
  section="Styleguide"
  description="The essay layout with sidenotes, as a specimen."
  variant="essay"
  noindex
>
  <Kicker date={today} />
  <h1>Essay specimen</h1>
  <p>
    Essays set their measure two columns in, so the margin to the right is narrower and the notes run
    tighter. Bush closed his 1945 essay on the record and whether we learn to use it.<SidenoteRef n={1} />
  </p>
  <Sidenote n={1}>
    Vannevar Bush, “As We May Think,” <i>The Atlantic Monthly</i>, July 1945, p. 108.
  </Sidenote>
  <p>
    A records request is one way to use it. The law gives a citizen the right to inspect and copy public
    records during the custodian's regular business hours.<SidenoteRef n={2} />
  </p>
  <Sidenote n={2}>
    <span class="mono">§ 25-19-105(a)(1)(A)</span>.
  </Sidenote>
  <p>
    This page exists to show the layout; its text is sample copy.
  </p>
</Periodical>
